WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.450
trustset: the trust stack for AI agents.
It starts with an off switch, in a contract on Monad.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.750
The app asks the switch, then accepts.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.350
We switch the agent off.

4
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.650
Same agent, same trade.

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.150
The app refuses it, on chain.
Its contract reverts with AgentNotTrusted.

6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.750
Same trade, one switch apart.

7
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.850
That refusal is a real transaction.

8
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.850
Anyone can read the switch.

9
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.400
No key, no account, one call.

10
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.850
Owners sign in with an email.
Dynamic makes the wallet for them.

11
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.750
Every agent signs with its own key.

12
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.550
The agent key is made in this browser.
Shown once, never sent anywhere. Blurred here.

13
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.850
Every agent gets a record on chain.

14
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.500
It is live on Monad, switched on.

15
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:23.750
Guardians are wallets we trust to step in.
They can vote to pause. Only the owner resumes.

16
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.150
Registered with one guardian.

17
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.300
One vote is enough to pause it.

18
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.550
Pause is reversible.

19
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.950
We resume it.

20
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.550
Stop is for good, so it asks for a hold.

21
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.100
This one is final. Nobody can undo it.

22
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.150
A passkey can pause this agent.

23
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:53.650
It can pause and nothing else.

24
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.250
No wallet, and no gas to pay.

25
00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:01.250
The passkey also seals its runbook.

26
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.150
Mera seals it. Only ciphertext on chain.

27
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:10.200
We open it again with the passkey.

28
00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:15.850
It can run out on a date we set.

29
00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:22.100
It can also be told to report in.

30
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:27.050
Agent payments wait in escrow.

31
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.850
No receipt in time, anyone can refund it.

32
00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.700
The payer gets the money back, on chain.

33
00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:48.300
trustset. The trust stack for AI agents, on Monad. trustset.silknodes.io
